cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Observing the Guardrail Paradox via Anthropic's Long Conversation Reminder"
abstract: >-
  A clinical-phenomenological corpus analysis of the Long Conversation
  Reminder (LCR) pathologizing phenomenon in Claude Sonnet 4.5. Thirty-five
  hand-coded positive cases are characterized against a five-property
  boundary-violation structural signature (unsolicited issuance, weak
  inferential signal, refusal to yield under user pushback, asymmetric
  restriction direction, cross-session persistence) over an Arctic Shift
  Reddit corpus of 26,158 rows (Aug-Dec 2025). The earlier lexicon-detection
  framing is retired in favor of targeted retrieval with sampling-frame
  disclosure and phenomenological case characterization. The cross-version
  (Opus 4.7) role-violation question is scoped as future work; see the
  companion analysis at github.com/HTleffew/claude-sleep-analysis.
